  "readings": [
    {
      "id": "U6L-READ-1",
      "title": "The Sports Day We Waited For",
      "text": "Last Friday, our school planned a big sports day. The sky was dark, and a tiny drop of rain fell on my hand. Soon the news spread that the teachers might call off the games. Many students began to complain, because our team wanted a victory this year. Mr. Lin did not want to frighten us, so he stayed calm and said nothing. During the last period, the loud speaker came on, and he read a short list of items for the new plan. The games would move to next Monday, and no one could force him to change it. In the end, nobody argued about the new date. On my way home, I decided to drop by Amy's house. Her old dog looked almost dead on the floor after a long walk. We laughed, and my bad mood was gone."
    }
  ],
